{# The contextual help button (ARCHITECTURE.md §8.64) — ALWAYS visible,
   included once, at the right of the breadcrumb bar
   (partials/breadcrumb_bar.html.twig), which since the mega-menu rework
   shows at every width, mobile, desktop browser and installed PWA alike.
   (The original plan doubled it into the desktop nav's right-hand group,
   back when the breadcrumb bar was hidden in a desktop browser tab —
   that would now put two identical buttons on screen at once.)

   ONE shape now, on every page: a <button> opening the offcanvas panel
   (partials/help_panel.html.twig, which base.html.twig renders
   unconditionally). It used to be a plain /aide link on a page no topic
   covered — the panel then had nothing to show. It always has something
   now: the search field is on top of it, works at every role and needs no
   network, and a page without its own topic is exactly where searching
   the corpus is most useful. The panel's own footer still links /aide for
   the full list.

   `route_help` is the Twig global Core\Http\FrontController sets after
   the RBAC guard — already role-filtered, already rendered — and decides
   only what the panel shows BELOW the search field, no longer whether the
   button opens anything. #}
<button type="button"
        class="btn btn-link p-1 border-0 text-body-secondary d-inline-flex align-items-center"
        data-bs-toggle="offcanvas"
        data-bs-target="#help-panel"
        aria-controls="help-panel"
        title="{% if route_help|default([]) is not empty %}Aide sur cette page{% else %}Aide{% endif %}">
    <i class="bi bi-question-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <span class="visually-hidden">{% if route_help|default([]) is not empty %}Aide sur cette page{% else %}Aide{% endif %}</span>
</button>
